# G078 — Media Player Widget

*v2. See `media-player.md` for prose: three-state FSM (Stopped ↔
Playing ↔ Paused), context-dependent transport actions, tick as the
engine, repeat × shuffle as orthogonal modes, events on boundaries
not every tick.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault-Scoped Background Music Channel

[music-channel @tag
    IN ORDER TO
        build a playlist from vault-tagged notes, start it with
        repeat-all and shuffle, and tick the engine on a real-time
        cadence while surfacing boundary events as UI updates

    @tracks   <- [vault[find-notes {tag: @tag}]]
                 mapped to [media[render-as-track {note: @n}]]
    @player   <- [media[new-player]]
    [media[load-playlist {player: @player, tracks: @tracks}]]
    [media[set-repeat   {player: @player, mode: "all"}]]
    [media[set-shuffle  {player: @player, on: true}]]
    [media[play {player: @player}]]

    every 100 ms
        @events <- [media[tick {player: @player, delta-ms: 100}]]
        for @e in @events
            @e where kind is "TrackStarted"
                -> [ui[update-now-playing {track: @e:track}]]
            @e where kind is "PlaylistEnded"
                -> [ui[toast {msg: "playlist cycled"}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[media
    new-player
    load-playlist      {player, tracks}
    set-repeat         {player, mode}                  ;; "none" | "one" | "all"
    set-shuffle        {player, on}
    play               {player}                         ;; context-dependent
    pause              {player}
    stop               {player}
    next               {player}
    previous           {player}
    tick               {player, delta-ms}               ;; -> [Event]
    position-ms        {player}
    current-track      {player}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: transport verb's effect dispatched by `where` state

[media[play {player: @p}]
    IN ORDER TO
        start playback from whatever "start" means in the current state
        so callers never have to query state before calling play

    @p:state
        where Stopped -> load track 0, state := Playing,
                         emit TrackStarted(0), StateChanged(Playing)
        where Paused  -> resume at current position, state := Playing,
                         emit StateChanged(Playing)
        where Playing -> no-op
]

FSM with state-interpreted operations (works in every state, does the
right thing) — contrast G062's state-gated (refuses if wrong state).

## Distinctive Innate idiom: tick loop consumes delta `where` boundaries fire events

[media[tick {player: @p, delta-ms: @dt}]
    IN ORDER TO
        advance position by @dt ms, crossing as many track boundaries
        as the delta covers, emitting events at each boundary

    @p where state is not Playing -> return [] (no-op)

    loop while @dt > 0
        @remaining-in-track <- track:duration-ms - @p:position-ms
        where @dt at least @remaining-in-track
            -> advance to track end (position := duration)
            -> emit TrackEnded(current)
            -> @next <- next-track-under (@p:repeat, @p:shuffle)
               where @next exists -> emit TrackStarted(@next), position := 0
               otherwise          -> emit PlaylistEnded, state := Stopped
            -> @dt := @dt - @remaining-in-track
        otherwise
            -> @p:position-ms += @dt
            -> @dt := 0
]

Events fire on boundaries, not every tick. UIs subscribe to events
for "now playing"; UIs poll position-ms for the scrubber. Two
different consumption patterns on the same engine output.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @p <- [media[new-player]]
    [media[load-playlist
            {player: @p,
             tracks: [{id: 0, duration-ms: 1000}
                      {id: 1, duration-ms: 1000}]}]]
    [media[set-repeat  {player: @p, mode: "all"}]]
    [media[play        {player: @p}]]

    -> [media[tick {player: @p, delta-ms: 3000}]]
    ;; -> [TrackEnded(0), TrackStarted(1),
    ;;     TrackEnded(1), TrackStarted(0),
    ;;     TrackEnded(0), TrackStarted(1)]
    ;;    (delta crossed 3 track boundaries under repeat=all)

    -> [media[position-ms {player: @p}]]     ;; -> 0
    -> [media[current-track {player: @p}]]   ;; -> track 1
]
